Subject: [PATCH 5/5] uapi: fcntl: define O_TMPFILE for Android 9 userspace

Building LineageOS 16.0 against this kernel stops at the display HAL:

    gralloc.msm8952_intermediates/gpu.o
    bionic/libc/include/bits/fortify/fcntl.h:63:26:
        error: use of undeclared identifier 'O_TMPFILE'

The Qualcomm HALs compile against the kernel's own exported headers
(KERNEL_OBJ/usr/include, from headers_install), which take precedence over
bionic's copies. O_TMPFILE arrived in Linux 3.11, so this 3.10 tree does not
define it, while Pie's bionic fortify header assumes it exists.

This adds the definition exactly as Linux 3.11 has it in
include/uapi/asm-generic/fcntl.h, comment included. It is header-only: nothing
in this kernel references O_TMPFILE, so the kernel's behaviour does not change.

And the definition is designed for exactly this situation. O_TMPFILE is
__O_TMPFILE | O_DIRECTORY, so on a kernel that does not implement it -- this
one -- the unknown bit is ignored and the open() is an O_DIRECTORY open with
write access, which fails with EISDIR. Userspace sees a clean failure and falls
back, instead of silently getting a regular file. Hence upstream's own comment,
"a horrid kludge trying to make sure that this will fail on old kernels".
---
diff --git include/uapi/asm-generic/fcntl.h include/uapi/asm-generic/fcntl.h
index a48937d4..d2940bbd 100644
--- include/uapi/asm-generic/fcntl.h
+++ include/uapi/asm-generic/fcntl.h
@@ -84,6 +84,14 @@
 #define O_PATH		010000000
 #endif
 
+#ifndef __O_TMPFILE
+#define __O_TMPFILE	020000000
+#endif
+
+/* a horrid kludge trying to make sure that this will fail on old kernels */
+#define O_TMPFILE (__O_TMPFILE | O_DIRECTORY)
+#define O_TMPFILE_MASK (__O_TMPFILE | O_DIRECTORY | O_CREAT)
+
 #ifndef O_NDELAY
 #define O_NDELAY	O_NONBLOCK
 #endif
